# Legal content (`web/content/`)

When editing legal pages (`privacy.*.md`, `terms.*.md`), keep statements aligned with real product behavior.

- Update **English and Russian** versions in the same change whenever possible.
- Keep legal claims consistent with implementation in:
  - `mobile/src/shared/lib/analytics.ts`
  - `mobile/src/shared/lib/crashlytics.ts`
  - `mobile/src/features/app-storefront/` and `mobile/src/features/yandex-interstitial/`
  - `mobile/src/features/entitlements/` and `web/app/api/pro-license/**`
  - `web/services/ai.service.ts`, `web/services/translate.service.ts`, `web/services/ask.service.ts`
  - `web/config/constants.ts` (TTL/rate-limit values)
- If behavior changes materially, update the **Last updated** date in legal docs.
- Avoid promising stricter guarantees than the code currently enforces.
